When you ask my gogo to pay R50 a month for an app that promises to pay me back for studying, it sounds exactly like the empty promises politicians make while our Pietermaritzburg infrastructure crumbles. I already spend over half an hour commuting to a school that keeps letting me down, and adding another R600 a year to our tight R10,000 monthly household budget just to chase a financial reward feels like a risk we cannot justify. I would only reconsider if Thuto.io was completely free to join and actually proved it could help me pass matric despite the poor teaching I receive.

