ECONOMIC: {"impulse": 0.1, "perceived_cost": "R600 annually on top of my R4000-R8000 school fees", "primary_objection": "Paying money to earn money sounds like another empty promise and doesn't fix why my school is failing me", "reconsider_condition": "The platform must be completely free and prove it can actually help me pass matric"}

The idea of earning actual money for studying sounds like a dream since my school here in Pietermaritzburg keeps letting us down, but paying R50 a month upfront is impossible when my grandmother's grant barely covers my transport for my half-hour commute and the data I buy for my phone. I cannot justify spending our tight food money on a subscription just for the chance to earn rewards, especially when I already struggle to afford the data needed to even load the app. If Thuto.io was completely free to join and only took a small percentage of the cash I actually earned, I would gladly use it during my long commute.

